# Commit, PR, and Jira

## Scope (read first)

This rule applies **only** to Intuit / work repositories.

If the current workspace is a **personal** project, **ignore this entire rule**. Use conventional commits with an emoji and **no Jira key**. Personal signals include:

- Paths under `Programming/Personal/` (or similar personal trees)
- Personal GitHub remotes / accounts (e.g. `github.com/sdc224/...`)
- Non-Intuit remotes and personal dotfiles

Do not append `DXS-*` (or any Intuit Jira key) to personal commits or PR titles.

## Commits (Intuit / work repos only)

Apply these whenever creating commits, pull requests, or Jira issues in work repos unless the user overrides them.

- Conventional Commits: `type(scope): subject`
- Include an emoji in the **title** after the colon
- **Scope is lowercase only** (package or area name). Never put a Jira key in the scope — keys are uppercase (`DXS-19505`) and commitlint rejects caps in scope.
- Put the Jira key at the **end of the title**, separated by a hyphen: ` - DXS-12345`
- Title (first line) **must be ≤ 70 characters**
- Body is optional; keep it to why, not a file list

Examples:

```
fix(storybook): 🔧 recover Storybook and bundle - DXS-19505
feat(release): ✨ add per-package release - DXS-19505
```

Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`.

## Pull requests (Intuit / work repos only)

- PR **title must match the commit title**, including the emoji and Jira key
- Do not drop the emoji when creating or editing the PR
- Body: short Summary + Test plan; include the Jira URL

## Jira (Intuit / work repos only)

- Default project: **DXS** (Data Extraction Services)
- Default type for this kind of work: **Story**
- Assign to the current user (Sourodeep Chatterjee)
- Set **Story Points** when asked (this recovery story is 5)
- Link a parent epic before In Progress (workflow requires it)
- Active DXS epic used for this work: **DXS-19317** (in2Doc Enhancements and support)
- Add to the current DXS sprint if In Progress rejects the transition
- Transition: Open → **Start Progress** (In Progress)
- Ticket for this modernization: **DXS-19505**
  https://intuit-prod.atlassian.net/browse/DXS-19505

## In2Doc design-system context

- Requirements / done / pending live in `docs/MODERNIZATION-CONTEXT.md`
- Keep monorepo component packages; do not create a new DevPortal asset
